---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { TERMS_VERSION } from "../../lib/board-terms";
---

<Layout
  title="Parish Board Terms | St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission"
  description="The terms for using the parish message board: conduct, posting, private messages, reporting and more."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:px-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-tan-dark">Parish Board</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl text-text-primary md:text-5xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 h-px w-24 bg-liturgical-current"></div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-text-secondary">Version {TERMS_VERSION}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      The parish board is where the people of St. John of Kronstadt Orthodox Mission, Bayview,
      Texas (&ldquo;the parish&rdquo;) talk with one another. By using it, you agree to what follows.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-8 mt-10 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-primary/85">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">1. Who can use the board</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The board is for catechumens and members of the parish, with the approval of the parish
          priest. Access can be given or taken away at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">2. Christian conduct</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Be considerate, honest and kind, the way you would be in the church hall. Do not harass,
          threaten, shame or bully anyone. Do not post hateful, abusive, sexual or violent material.
          Do not pretend to be someone else. Do not use the board for spam, advertising or selling.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">3. You are responsible for what you post</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          What you post, in a topic or in a private message, is your own and you are responsible for
          it. The parish does not write it and does not endorse it, and what members say does not
          speak for the parish. Once a message is sent, it can't be edited or deleted by itself.
          Think before you send.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">4. Posting rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          By posting, you let the board show what you post to the people who can use it. Only post
          photos and words you have the right to share. Do not post photos of other people's
          children without a parent's permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">5. Moderators and removal</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Moderators and admins may remove any post, photo or topic, close a topic, and remove
          someone's access to the board, at their discretion and without warning when they think it is
          needed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">6. Private messages</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Private messages are private between the people in them. No page on the board lets anyone
          else read them. They are kept on the parish's site as ordinary text and are not encrypted.
          A conversation is removed from the site once everyone in it has cleared it from their
          inbox. Individual messages can't be edited or deleted.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If someone reports a conversation, a copy of the whole conversation is saved and read by the
          site's admins. An admin may also open a private conversation in an emergency, or if the law
          requires it. Each time an admin opens one, the time and the reason are recorded in a log
          that every admin can see.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">7. Reporting and ignoring</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Use Report on a private conversation if something said in it is wrong or frightening. If
          you ignore someone, nothing from them reaches you and they aren't told. Only a moderator or
          admin can lift an ignore, so choose it carefully. Moderators and admins can't be ignored.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">8. In an emergency</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The board is not for emergencies and is not watched around the clock. If someone is in
          danger, call 911. Threats of harm may be reported to law enforcement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">9. No guarantees</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The board is provided as it is, without promises that it will always work, always be
          available, or keep everything posted to it. To the fullest extent the law allows, the
          parish is not responsible for what members post or do, for what happens between members, or
          for any loss from using the board.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">10. Changes, and ending the board</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The parish may change these terms, or change or close the board, at any time. When the terms
          change, you'll be asked to agree again. Using the board after that means you accept the new
          terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">11. Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">12. Members under 18</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Young people are welcome on the board. A member under 18 uses it with a parent's or
          guardian's permission, and by letting them use it, the parent or guardian agrees to these
          terms for them.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div id="end-of-terms"></div>

    <section id="agree-panel" class="hidden mt-12 border border-border-soft bg-cream-card p-5">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary">Agree to the Terms</h2>
      <p id="agree-hint" class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
        You've read to the end. Tick the box, then press the button to enter the board.
      </p>
      <label class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-3 text-base">
        <input id="agree-check" type="checkbox" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5" />
        <span>I have read the Terms of Use and I agree to them.</span>
      </label>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <button
          id="agree-btn"
          type="button"
          disabled
          class="bg-text-primary px-5 py-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-cream-bg disabled:opacity-40"
        >
          Agree and enter the board
        </button>
        <span id="agree-status" class="ml-3 text-sm" role="status"></span>
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-text-secondary">
      Questions? Call <a href="tel:+19564346874">(956) 434-6874</a> or use the
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  const panel = document.getElementById("agree-panel") as HTMLElement;
  const check = document.getElementById("agree-check") as HTMLInputElement;
  const button = document.getElementById("agree-btn") as HTMLButtonElement;
  const status = document.getElementById("agree-status") as HTMLElement;
  const end = document.getElementById("end-of-terms") as HTMLElement;

  async function start() {
    let state: { agreed: boolean; version: string };
    try {
      const res = await fetch("/api/board/agree", { credentials: "same-origin", cache: "no-store" });
      if (!res.ok) return; // not signed in, or not on the board: just reading
      state = await res.json();
    } catch {
      return;
    }
    if (state.agreed) return;

    panel.classList.remove("hidden");
    // The box only works once they have scrolled to the end of the terms.
    check.disabled = true;
    const hint = document.getElementById("agree-hint") as HTMLElement;
    hint.textContent = "Please read the Terms above to the end. Then you can tick the box and agree.";
    const unlock = () => {
      check.disabled = false;
      hint.textContent = "You've read to the end. Tick the box, then press the button to enter the board.";
    };
    new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
      if (entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) {
        unlock();
        obs.disconnect();
      }
    }).observe(end);

    check.addEventListener("change", () => {
      button.disabled = !check.checked;
    });
    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      button.disabled = true;
      status.textContent = "Saving…";
      const res = await fetch("/api/board/agree", {
        method: "POST",
        credentials: "same-origin",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ version: state.version }),
      });
      if (!res.ok) {
        button.disabled = false;
        status.textContent = "Couldn't save that. Please try again.";
        return;
      }
      const next = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("next") ?? "";
      window.location.assign(next.startsWith("/board/") ? next : "/board/");
    });
  }
  start();
</script>
